A||||16||kiss||vibration over 55||||1||
Z||000000||kiss||07-15-2001||10:36 AM||||new shocks,two alignments,balanced tires,new bushings,ball joints and a new rack! the steering still vibrates over 55 mph. what's up with that? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||07-15-2001||10:59 AM||||What work was done on the rear? The tie rod ends could be bad, Struts, bearings, bent wheel, worn motor/trans mounts, worn cradle bushings, bad CV joint in rear, etc<BR>Due to the suspension lay-out if something is bad in the back it could vibrate the front too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||kiss||07-15-2001||11:49 AM||||new struts,new tires and rims,springs. bushing are not new but in good cond. no bent parts.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||07-15-2001||12:53 PM||||Is there any play in the steering column?  Maybe the u-joint ath the end?<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||07-15-2001||01:20 PM||||Get an on the car spin balancing check...<BR>  Also check the wheel bearings, front and rear...<BR>    crash...||||reg||1
Z||000005||LivoniaFieroGT||07-15-2001||02:39 PM||||Had similar vibration and went thru all the traditional checks.  Come to find out the rack shock dampener (GM p/n 22046471) was bad.  Try that.<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000006||kiss||07-15-2001||02:58 PM||||joints have been checked and no dampener it's a 88.im stumped!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||07-15-2001||04:31 PM||||I was just about to post the same question (vibration over 55). I always had a little play in the steering wheel (not real play, just a kind of <I>deadzone</I> where the front wheels are less reactive to the steering wheel) but the vibration just got <u>much</u> worse. It also feels like the car is <I>searching</I> from left to right a bit. It's hard to keep it in a straight line. When I let go of the steering wheel, it doesn't pull to one side, it will continue to go from left to right. Any ideas on that? Could that be the rack shock dampener as well?||||reg||1
Z||000008||kiss||07-15-2001||04:52 PM||||that's the rack-gears (teeth) could be worn.<BR>get it checked out!||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||07-15-2001||07:15 PM||||have the tire installer check the tire runout while you watch. Ive bought several sets of tires in last few years that were bad. (out of round) I went thru 3 sets on Mercedes before they got a good set, 2 sets on my kit Fiero. I dont think the dampener has anything to do with it. I dont even have one at all on mine. runs smooth up n over 150mph Mine were also spin balanced ON the car.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||07-15-2001||07:41 PM||||Cliff, It may not be the rack gears but could be worn end bushings on the rack. Stock they are plastic, aftermarket units have brass bushings. I think you can buy just the brass bushings. Rodney sells them in aluminum.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/n18.html" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com/n18.html</A> <P>When they wear out the passenger inner tie rod get "sloppy" and can cause what you are describing. Also Rodney sell a kit to rebuild the rack if you want to replace the pilot bearings and such.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cliff Pennock||07-15-2001||08:03 PM||||How long would it take to replace a steering rack bushing? I read on Rodney's site you have to remove the rack and completely take it apart...||||reg||1
Z||000012||Oreif||07-15-2001||09:43 PM||||To rebuild the rack would take about a day.<BR>Once it is out of the car it would take 2 hours to rebuild. Figure about an hour to get the rack out, fix broken bolts (If they break) and an hour back in. We swapped a rack that was broken and it took about 4 hours to do because the collar to the steering column was a pain to get off and on. (Limited space to work with.) Plus we had to drill-out one broken bolt.<BR>Spray bolts with a penetrating spray to avoid breaking bolts. It would also be a good time to replace the tie rod ends since it's all apart too. If replacing the tie rod ends, just meaure the distance from the end of the rack to the tie rod end so you can install the new ones and get the alignment close.||||reg||1
Z||000013||GTMike||07-16-2001||12:37 AM||||i have a similare problem.  mine fiverats at around 75.  i'm haveing the tires ballanced tomarrow and a alingment.  i hope it clears it up.  the wierd thing is.  it starts in the front  i feel it in the stearing wheel then it comes back to the back. of the car.  and then moves back to the front.   kinda wierd. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cliff Pennock||07-16-2001||05:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GTMike:<BR><B>i have a similare problem.  mine fiverats at around 75.  i'm haveing the tires ballanced tomarrow and a alingment.  i hope it clears it up.  the wierd thing is.  it starts in the front  i feel it in the stearing wheel then it comes back to the back. of the car.  and then moves back to the front.   kinda wierd. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's <u>exactly</u> what my car is doing now. First my dash and steering wheel starts to vibrate, then that stops and I can see my door vibrate violently, than that stops and I can see my rear wing vibrate in the mirror. Very weird indeed.||||reg||1
Z||000015||GTMike||07-16-2001||06:14 PM||||wow are you kidding me  this exactly what mine is doing.  i mean  exactly.   so i got the tires ballanced today. and i think it helped a little.   but i might just be getting use to it.   <P>its not a viloent shake. but i can see my doors wiggle and i can see the ends of the wing wiggleing too.   could it  be warn struts?     <P>my stearing is perfect  i have 0 play in the wheel  my alingment is perfect too. it doesn't wonder or pull at all.   i had her up to over 120 to day testing out my new ballanced tires and the stearing was perfect.     <P>i called and alingment shop and asked them about it and they said the  the alingment wont affect  shimmy or shake.    <P>also  its only at 77-84ish.    not at rpms  the rpms are smooth  so i know its not any mounts or the engine shaking.<P>any one have ideas???<p>[This message has been edited by GTMike (edited 07-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cliff Pennock||07-16-2001||08:18 PM||||I'm also worried if this is dangerous or not. I don't like going into a turn to find out the car will not.||||reg||1
